<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating expected profit for micro-business insurance policies</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Bima Salama Insurance offers a fire protection policy for micro-business owners in Nakuru. The company charges an annual premium of <b>KES {@premium@}</b> per policy.</p>

<p>If a fire occurs, the insurance company pays out a compensation claim of <b>KES {@payout@}</b>. Based on historical county data, the probability of a micro-business making a fire claim in a given year is \(\displaystyle \frac{{@claim_rate@}}{1000}\).</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Calculate the expected payout (the average financial risk to the insurance company) for a single policy.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an exact number of KES).</i></p>
<p>\(\text{Expected Payout} =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Calculate the expected profit the insurance company makes on a single policy.</p>
<p>\(\text{Expected Profit} =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> If the company successfully sells <b>{@num_policies@}</b> policies this year, what is their total projected expected profit?</p>
<p>\(\text{Total Profit} =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Expected Payout</b><br>
The expected value of an event is the probability of the event multiplied by its financial outcome. The company only pays out if a fire occurs.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Expected Payout} = P(\text{Claim}) \times \text{Payout Amount} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Expected Payout} = \frac{{@claim_rate@}}{1000} \times {@payout@} = {@ta1@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Expected Payout} = \text{KES } {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Expected Profit per Policy</b><br>
The expected profit is the money the company collects (the premium) minus the money it expects to pay out on average.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Expected Profit} = \text{Premium} - \text{Expected Payout} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Expected Profit} = {@premium@} - {@ta1@} = {@ta2@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Expected Profit} = \text{KES } {@ta2@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part c: Total Projected Profit</b><br>
To find the total profit for multiple policies, multiply the expected profit per policy by the number of policies sold.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Total Profit} = \text{Expected Profit per Policy} \times \text{Number of Policies} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Total Profit} = {@ta2@} \times {@num_policies@} = {@ta3@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Total Profit} = \text{KES } {@ta3@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
